From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:21:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sessions): let agents page session history and find
 recent sessions

Carried on custom until upstream answers the feature request for it
(not opened yet) and a PR merges.

Agents that review past sessions (e.g. a scheduled retro) could only list
sessions in creation order with no timestamps, and could only read the
last 50 items of a session, so walking a long transcript or finding what
changed since the previous run was impossible.

- sys_session_list: optional updated_after (ISO-8601), order_by
  (created|updated) and ownership (any|mine|shared) filters for the
  global view; each row now reports created_at, updated_at and owner.
  Backed by a new updated_after query param on GET /v1/sessions.
- sys_session_get_history: optional order='asc' and an 'after' item
  cursor read forward from the start or from a saved position, reusing
  GET /v1/sessions/{id}/items. Results carry next_cursor and has_more,
  plus has_older on a most-recent read; an unresolvable cursor returns
  invalid_cursor. Imports the database layer only when a history read
  needs it, so host startup stays free of it.
  Defaults, the tail_items cap and the character budget are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
